known_false_positives.description:
orientation_text_to_enum_value returns `0` on unknown input. This silently maps to a possibly valid enum value depending on definition, and may hide configuration errors. Prefer returning a safe default like `LV_SWITCH_ORIENTATION_AUTO` (or current orientation), and/or assert/log and keep existing value rather than forcing 0.

```suggestion
    LV_LOG_WARN("%s is an unknown value for switch orientation", txt);
        return LV_SWITCH_ORIENTATION_AUTO;
```
